<title>UK: British beet test shows 112.7 g sugar per root.</title>
<headline>British beet test shows 112.7 g sugar per root.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are details of the eighth British sugar beet test, carried out on Monday September 23 and issued by British Sugar Plc.</p>
<p>			    8TH TEST 96  8TH TEST 95  5-YR AVG</p>
<p> SUGAR GRAMS/ROOT	   632	    573	    634</p>
<p> SUGAR CONTENT (PCT)    17.84	  15.80	  17.22</p>
<p> ROOT WEIGHT (GRAMS)    112.7	   90.5	  109.2</p>
<p>&quot;The crop continues to make good progress. It remains on course for an average result, however it is now in need of more rain,&quot; British Sugar said in a statement. -- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4985</p>
</text>
